  "body": "### What\n\nThe Rust COM API uses futures for asynchronous stream and notification support. The public Subscription::to_stream() API returns a futures::Stream; the LoLa runtime uses futures::task::AtomicWaker to notify pending receives when samples arrive. The mock runtime also uses stream helpers and an executor in its support code.\n\nThis is used in API/runtime behavior, unlike a build-only procedural macro dependency. The COM API does not require application users to adopt a particular executor.\n\nAcceptance criteria\n\n- Record the pinned crate version, enabled features, and direct COM API call sites.\n- Distinguish production runtime use from mock/test-only use.\n- Review crate provenance, license, maintenance status, and safety relevance.\n- Document whether to retain futures, reduce its use, or replace specific functionality, and record the required qualification artifacts.\n\n### How\n\n_No response_\n\n### Estimates for realization\n\n_No response_\n\n### Category\n\n- [ ] Affects Detailed Design\n\n### Requirements / Architecture\n\n- [x] Requirements / Architecture are not affected by this change?",
